title: Vera Economic Conference
subtitle: The great realms convene at Vera to tackle the calamity...
view-if: year = 1933 and month >= 6
on-arrival: london_economic_conference_seen = 1
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
go-to: economic_recovery if disfavored < 15; no_recovery if disfavored >= 15
tags: event

= Vera Economic Conference

# TODO: if you've recovered, you get economic recovery
# if you haven't recovered, you can either back devaluation or back Ethia/Fulyria's fixed rates

Ethia has convened the realms at Vera to discuss the state of the continental economy and possible solutions to the ongoing calamity. All want to reduce tariffs to encourage trade. But the great powers are at an impasse: <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> and, to a lesser extent, <span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyria</span> are calling for fixed currency exchange rates, while the merchant-lords of the Allied States want to print new money to stimulate demand, calling for "controlled inflation". The debtor-realms — Ethia and the Commonwealth among them — seek relief on what they owe the Allied States' merchant-lords, who favor continued full payment.

@economic_recovery

[? if wtb_adopted or budget <= 0: the Commonwealth has largely recovered from the crisis, owing in large part to the same sorts of economic policies that the reformers is pursuing. ?]
[? if not wtb_adopted and budget > 0: the Commonwealth has largely recovered from the crisis, without having to resort to budget deficits or devaluing the currency. ?]

- @support_roosevelt
- @support_france
- @stable_currency_out_of_gov
- @salvage
- @no_business

@no_recovery

the Commonwealth, like the rest of the world, is still deep in the economic crisis, even if it has appeared to bottom out.

- @support_roosevelt
- @support_france
- @stable_currency_out_of_gov
- @salvage
- @no_business


@stable_currency_out_of_gov
title: Commonwealth representatives call for stable currency, along with <span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyria</span> and <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>.
view-if: not marcher_in_government
on-arrival: west_relation += 1

As expected, the conservative Commonwealth bankers support <span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyria</span> and <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>'s plan to stabilize currency exchange rates. In response to the continued support for fixed currency exchange rates and the impasse on debts, the Allied States pull out of the conference, leaving it with no agreements whatsoever.

[? if disfavored >= 15 : Nevertheless, the world economy is slowly improving due in part to the economic stimulus and more liberal trade policies of the reformist powers. ?]
[? if disfavored < 15 : Nevertheless, the world economy is slowly improving due in part to the economic stimulus and more liberal trade policies of the reformist powers as well as our own economic plan. ?]


@support_roosevelt
title: Support the reformers' ideas - we must devalue currency.
view-if: marcher_in_government


We support the reformers' plan for controlled inflation, leaving us at odds with the continental powers. In response to the continued support for fixed currency exchange rates by <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> and <span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyria</span> and the impasse on debts, the Allied States pull out of the conference, leaving it with no agreements whatsoever.

@support_france
title: Support <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> and <span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyria</span> - we must have stable currency.
view-if: marcher_in_government
on-arrival: west_relation += 1; eu_progress += 1

Our position brings us closer to other continental powers. In response to the continued support for fixed currency exchange rates and the impasse on debts, the Allied States pull out of the conference, leaving it with no agreements whatsoever.


@salvage
title: Can we try to salvage the negotiations?
view-if: marcher_in_government

How should we try to salvage the negotiations?

- @salvage_currency: Try to convince <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> and <span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyria</span> that slowly controlled inflation is possible and desirable.
- @salvage_debts: Try to convince the Allied States to reduce war debts for the sake of peace.
- @no_business: Nothing can be done.

@salvage_currency
choose-if: woytinsky_advisor = 1 and wtb_implemented > 1
unavailable-subtitle: Valdemar Voss would be extremely helpful right now.
on-arrival: foreign_aid = 1; disfavored -= 2 if disfavored >= 10; disfavored -= 1.5 if disfavored >= 5; inflation += 1.5; commons_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); burgher_marcher += 3*(1-dissent); economic_growth += 1.5 if economic_growth < 3

Valdemar Voss, now part of our delegation to the conference, uses our successful implementation of the Voss Renewal Plan in order to argue for loosening currency valuation. The argument is at least somewhat convincing, and an agreement is reached, leading to increased inflation and demand stimulus throughout the world.

@salvage_debts
choose-if: war_loans <= -2 and pacifism >= 3 and (rearmament_exposed or west_relation >= 3)
unavailable-subtitle: We cannot argue for pacifism in our current state.
on-arrival: foreign_aid = 1; budget += 1; disfavored -= 1 if disfavored >= 10; disfavored -= 1 if disfavored >= 5; inflation += 1 if inflation < 0; burgher_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); commons_marcher += 3*(1-dissent); economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth < 3

We try to argue that reducing war debts will reduce the risk of a future continental war, using our successful disarmament and the reduction in War Loan payments as an argument. The argument is at least somewhat convincing to the Allied States, leading to an agreement to reduce debts from the Great Wars. This indirectly also improves our economy.

@no_business
title: This conference is none of our concern.
view-if: marcher_in_government

The conference collapses, as expected. In response to the continued support for fixed currency exchange rates and the impasse on debts, the Allied States pull out of the conference, leaving it with no agreements whatsoever.

[? if disfavored >= 15 : Nevertheless, the world economy is slowly improving due in part to the economic stimulus and more liberal trade policies of the reformist powers. ?]
[? if disfavored < 15 : Nevertheless, the world economy is slowly improving due in part to the economic stimulus and more liberal trade policies of the reformist powers as well as our own economic plan. ?]